================================================================================
ASSETS NOTICE - READ THIS BEFORE PUBLISHING A BUILD
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers the source code in this repository: the Ren'Py
script files, the Python asset pipeline under tools/, and the documentation.

It does NOT cover the generated art and audio in game/images, game/gui,
game/audio and game/fonts, because those files are rendered from the graphics
and sounds inside DOOM2.WAD. DOOM, DOOM II, the DOOM logo, the monster and
weapon sprites, the textures, the STCFN font and the MUS soundtrack are
copyright (c) id Software LLC, a ZeniMax Media company, and remain the
property of their owners.

This project is a non-commercial fan work. It is intended for personal,
local use, exactly like a source port that asks you to supply your own IWAD.

If you intend to redistribute a build, regenerate the assets from an IWAD
that is freely redistributable - FreeDoom is the sane choice:

    python tools/build_assets.py --iwad freedoom2.wad --out .

FreeDoom is distributed under a BSD-style license and its assets can be
redistributed with attribution. See docs/ASSETS.md for the full breakdown.

The Cyrillic bitmap fonts are rasterisations of glyphs from DejaVu Sans
(Bitstream Vera license, free to modify and redistribute); only the rasterised
bitmaps are shipped, and they are generated, not copied from the IWAD.

Ren'Py itself is (c) Tom Rothamel and contributors, licensed under the MIT
license; it is not bundled in this repository.